  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on comparing variances and favoring lower variance. The individual, however, focuses on the maximum possible outcome and its desirability in the absence of downside risk. The information considered by the individual (presence of zero as the worst outcome, higher reward in Lottery B) does not align with variance calculations. The justification (preferring higher reward with lower probability when no losses are possible) contradicts the variance-minimizing logic, which would favor Lottery A due to its lower variance. There is no indication that the individual computed or considered outcome dispersion. Therefore, the decision reason based on variance is not reflected in the deliberation.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
